# Docker, Alembic & Scripts

## Docker

- **Project name:** `cooking`. All commands use `docker compose -p cooking` so only this project is affected.
- **Containers:** `cooking-db`, `cooking-redis`, `cooking-adminer`, `cooking-api`, `cooking-worker`, `cooking-beat`. No separate migrate container; migrations run via the API container.
- Ports (if defaults are in use): Postgres 5433, Redis 6380, API 8001, Adminer 8081. Keep these in sync with `.env.example` and docs.

## Alembic

- **Migrations live in** `alembic/` (env.py, script.py.mako, versions/). `alembic.ini` has `script_location = alembic`.
- **Engine URL:** Use the app DB URL from config (e.g. in env.py: `config.get_main_option("sqlalchemy.url")` set from `settings.DATABASE_URL`), not the placeholder in alembic.ini.
- Run migrations: `docker compose -p cooking run --rm api alembic upgrade head` (same as in setup.sh).

## Scripts

- **setup.sh:** Prepare env, build images, bring up db + redis, wait for Postgres, run migrations via api container, then instruct user to run start.sh.
- **start.sh:** `docker compose -p cooking up -d`, then `docker compose -p cooking logs -f`.
- **stop.sh:** `docker compose -p cooking down`.
- Scripts must not start or stop services outside this project (rely on `-p cooking`).
